# Skip Routine Builds

Production builds are slow. Do **not** run `bun run build`, `next build`, or similar full build commands after routine code changes unless the user explicitly asks or the task truly requires it.

## Default after edits

- Rely on the editor/linter for quick feedback (`read_lints` on changed files).
- Do not run a build to "verify" styling, layout, copy, or small refactors.

## When a build is appropriate

Run a build only if:

- The user asks to build, deploy, or confirm the production bundle.
- You changed build tooling (`next.config`, `tsconfig`, bundler plugins, env used at build time).
- A prior change clearly broke compilation and lighter checks are insufficient.

## Faster alternatives (prefer these)

| Need | Use instead of build |
|------|----------------------|
| Type errors | `bunx tsc --noEmit` (only if types are in question) |
| Lint/format | linter on touched files |
| Runtime behavior | dev server if already running; otherwise describe what to check |

## Do not

- Run `bun run build` at the end of every task as a habit.
- Claim "build passed" without having run one when verification was skipped — say what was checked instead.
